// PENDING (not wired into run_tests.sh) — the reproducer for the nameless-constructor hole. See
// docs/ROADMAP.md §1 "Retire the nameless-constructor emission path".
//
// SPEC § Construction: "Nothing is constructible by default. A type with no `ctor` and no `of`/`zero`
// opt-in cannot be built." `Empty` has none of those, so BOTH lines below must be hard errors. Today they
// are ACCEPTED: `checkNamelessNewBanned` only rejects when the type has named ctors or the call has
// arguments, so a type with no constructor at all slips through and emits a bare `_F4__Empty b;` — no ctor
// call, no `= {0}`, no drop tracking. The program then reads uninitialized stack.
//
// It is also an escape hatch around `slot`: kama sees an initializer, so the M3 rule ("a local with no
// initializer must say `slot`") never fires, and clang's -Werror=uninitialized cannot see it either
// because the local is struct-typed.
//
// When fixed, this becomes two tests/xfail/ fixtures (one per form) and this file goes away.
import std::memory::{Owned};

type value Empty { public int32 v; }

fn int main() {
    Empty b = Empty();                 // MUST be an error — no ctor, no `of`/`zero` opt-in
    Owned<Empty> h = new Empty();      // MUST be an error — same, on the heap path
    return b.v;                        // reads uninitialized stack today
}
